{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to the command-line interface and expands the core specification capabilities with new operators for iteration, invocation, and data filling. It also improves the developer experience by ensuring all public specifier types provide meaningful string representations for debugging and introspection.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The glom CLI must accept Python-full specifications rather than being limited to AST literals, allowing for more complex logic in spec definitions. Additionally, the CLI should support targets that are AST literals, enabling direct usage of literal data structures as input sources."
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "text": "The library must expose new specification types including Iter, Invoke, Fill, Let, and Auto to handle streaming, callable invocation, default value filling, variable capture, and automatic mode selection respectively. The tuple steps must now nest scopes, allowing inner operations to access variables defined in outer scopes within the same tuple."
    },
    {
      "id": "m33",
      "text": "The string representation of Invoke expressions must be shortened to improve readability while still conveying necessary information about the invocation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m34",
      "text": "The internal arguments attribute of Invoke must be privatized to prevent external modification, and documentation should reflect the use of 'constants' instead of 'consts' for related module attributes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m44",
      "text": "The Fill specifier must implement a __repr__ method that returns a clear, human-readable string describing the fill operation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m45",
      "text": "The Assign specifier and its convenience function must implement a __repr__ method that clearly indicates the assignment being performed."
    },
    {
      "id": "m46",
      "text": "The Coalesce specifier must implement a __repr__ method that displays the coalescing logic, and the Inspect type must also have a reasonable representation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m47",
      "text": "The Check specifier and the Auto specifier must both implement __repr__ methods, ensuring that all public specifier types in the library now have reasonable string representations."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure these behaviors are verified against the public API surface before tagging the release."
}
